One day, a young girl named Lily decided to investigate. She had grown up hearing stories about the old house and was determined to uncover its secrets. With a flashlight in hand, she snuck through the overgrown garden and climbed the rickety stairs to the front door.

As she pushed open the door, she was hit by a musty scent that filled her nostrils. The inside of the house was in complete disarray, with cobwebs hanging from the ceiling and furniture overturned. But Lily didn't let that deter her. She began to search every nook and cranny of the house, her heart racing with anticipation.

As she made her way up the stairs, she heard a faint noise coming from the second floor. She followed the sound until she reached a door at the end of the hallway. She slowly pushed it open and was met with a sight that took her breath away.

In the center of the room was an old chest, its lid open to reveal a treasure trove of jewels and gold coins. Lily's eyes widened with excitement as she realized that she had stumbled upon the long-lost fortune of the previous owner.

But as she reached out to grab the treasure, she felt a hand on her shoulder. She spun around to find a shadowy figure standing behind her. Her heart raced as she tried to make out the face of the stranger, but it was too dark to see anything.

Suddenly, the figure spoke in a low, menacing voice, "That treasure is mine. Leave now and never come back."

Lily didn't argue. She quickly gathered her things and fled the house, her heart pounding in her chest. She knew that she had uncovered a secret that was better left hidden. And she also knew that the old house at the end of the street would always hold a mystery that no one would ever discover.
